{"ts":"2026-08-26T20:06:09.002Z","author":"claude","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"f559dcd5a5f387bc7221097a","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"Two plausible directions: batch the routing assertions into a single CLI invocation, or drive the routing contract from the command registry directly rather than through repeated process spawns. Raising a timeout would hide the sensitivity rather than remove it."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"ops-gp0d"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"A thirty-five second CLI test fails on timing whenever the machine is busy, so the gate reports red for load rather than for code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The test named installed pm CLI routes --repos values to every fleet command spawns the installed pm binary many times in sequence and takes roughly 30 to 35 seconds on an idle machine. It failed twice today while six packages full gate suites ran in parallel, and passed on the same commit both times when run alone, and also passed on main under the same parallel load conditions in one of the two comparisons. Nothing about the change under review touches the code paths it exercises. A gate that long is load sensitive by construction, so a red result from a parallel sweep cannot be distinguished from a real regression without a second serial run, which costs another half minute every time it happens."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":3},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["ci","flake","test"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-26T20:06:09.002Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-26T20:06:09.002Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/deadline","value":"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/assignee","value":"claude"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"claude"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The test either bounds its own runtime independently of machine load, or spawns the CLI once and asserts over the batch rather than once per command, so that a busy machine cannot turn it red"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-26T20:06:09.002Z","author":"claude","text":"Not introduced by the trusted-publishing change; that change touches only release.yml and its own test file."}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-26T20:06:09.002Z","author":"claude","text":"Observed three times on 2026-08-26: two failures under six-way parallel gate runs, one pass alone on the identical commit."}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/learnings","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-26T20:06:09.002Z","author":"claude","text":"A red result from a parallel gate sweep needs re-running in isolation before it is believed, whenever any single test takes tens of seconds."}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/files","value":[{"path":"test","scope":"project"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tests","value":[{"command":"npx tsx --test test/fleet-commands.test.ts","scope":"project"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/docs","value":[{"path":"https://nodejs.org/api/test.html#test-runner-execution-model","scope":"project","note":"node test runner concurrency and timing"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"87510313df8add56e65e7bf91c08f6884623bd910a5afc948a88aff2eb728d44","item_hash_version":2,"message":"Record the load-sensitive CLI routing test","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
