{"ts":"2026-08-26T22:15:53.550Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"66f51baccd944ab11404f28c","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-26T22:15:53.550Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The test named installed pm CLI routes --repos values to every fleet command spawns the installed pm binary many times in sequence and takes roughly 30 to 35 seconds on an idle machine. On 2026-08-26 UTC it failed twice while six packages full gate suites ran in parallel, and passed when re-run alone on the same commit. It also passed on main under comparable parallel load. The conclusion is that the test is load sensitive rather than broken, so a red result from a parallel sweep must be re-run in isolation before it is believed."}],"before_hash":"d71a1156e3a31cce85e1e899f2062dff7e868f65e0a2216114e222821dc503ea","after_hash":"ed3a9b0338e96e49254391917b49fdd3aecf728e5abde5eb27bdfa3bb3a9c4d4","item_hash_version":2,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
{"ts":"2026-08-26T22:15:54.161Z","author":"claude","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"66f51baccd944ab11404f28c","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-26T22:15:54.161Z","author":"claude","text":"Corrected an internal inconsistency this record carried: the description claimed the commit passed in isolation on both re-runs while the note recorded a single isolated pass among three observations. Those cannot both be right and I cannot re-derive which from the surviving evidence, so both now state only what is defensible - two failures under six-way parallel load, and a pass when re-run alone on the same commit - without asserting a count of isolated re-runs that the records disagree about. Inconsistent evidence is worse than less evidence, because it misleads flake triage."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-26T22:15:54.161Z"}],"before_hash":"ed3a9b0338e96e49254391917b49fdd3aecf728e5abde5eb27bdfa3bb3a9c4d4","after_hash":"9219b9ecde033550cd3e49b98da1d1033a794e200e28fe1e7a8cc4555d222789","item_hash_version":2,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
